+**Decentralised load fairness:** Freenet's next-generation routing learned
+per-peer response-time estimates over keyspace and, after a network-wide
+congestive collapse in 2003, imposed adaptive per-peer request quotas
+[Clarke et al. 2001; Clarke 2004]. Its author identified the missing
+mechanism as persistent accounting — an over-consumer should "build up a
+debt to the network" to be repaid under later contention [Clarke 2004]. The
+P2PCP earn–burn loop (Section 10.2.4) implements exactly such a ledger:
+work-priced participation, transferable credit, and deterministic replay
+supplying the verification that statistical peer-trust could not.
 
